WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
Stand facing a distant
cliff and shout.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.510
A moment later, your own
voice comes back to you.

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.170
Nobody shouted back.

4
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.910
The cliff simply returned your sound.

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.130
Ships and scanners use the same trick,

6
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.010
but with sound so high-pitched
that no human can hear it.

7
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.850
How can a delay measure a distance,

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.670
and why use sound we cannot hear?

9
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.410
In this mission, you'll see why
sound is a longitudinal wave

10
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.410
that needs something
to travel through.

11
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.470
You'll find the range of
frequencies human ears can hear,

12
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.650
and put echoes and ultrasound to work.

13
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.790
Your mission: find out how an
echo can measure a distance.
